@startuml
' Authority: Derived visual; accepted flow sections and ADRs control.
title FGA zero-state private-MVP activation, upload, and durable group handoff

hide footbox
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center

actor Administrator as Admin
actor Photographer as User
participant "FGA User UI browser\n(any trusted host for Part 1;\ntarget workstation for Part 2)" as AdminBrowser
participant "Client browser\n(optional manual admin use)" as ClientBrowser
participant "Windows current clipboard\n(history/sync off for transfer)" as Clipboard
participant "Windows\nDNS Client/cache" as ClientDNS
participant "Configured\nrecursive DNS" as RecursiveDNS
participant "Lightroom Classic" as LrC
participant "FGA LrC plug-in" as Plugin
database "LrPasswords" as Passwords
database "Plug-in local\nrecovery store" as Recovery
participant "FGA administrative\ncontrol plane" as Control
participant "Configured OIDC\nidentity provider" as OIDC
participant "FGA OAuth handler" as OAuth
participant "FGA API backend\nflickrgroupaddr.com" as API
database "FGA database" as DB
database "FGA managed Flickr\nsecret store" as Secrets
participant "Hosted DNS" as HostedDNS
participant "Flickr OAuth / REST API\nwww.flickr.com" as FlickrAPI
participant "Flickr upload API\nup.flickr.com" as FlickrUpload
participant "FGA refresh worker" as RefreshWorker
participant "Periodic due-work\nscheduler" as Scheduler
participant "FGA group-submission worker" as GroupWorker

note over ClientBrowser
  The FGA LrC plug-in never launches or controls this browser.
  Part 1 administration may use any trusted device.
  Part 2 uses a clean private window on the target workstation.
end note

== Phase 1, Part 0 — Authenticate the administrative browser ==

Admin -> AdminBrowser: Open https://flickrgroupaddr.com/admin/
AdminBrowser -> Control: GET /admin/login
Control -> Control: Apply shared source + deployment buckets\n+ 20-live-transaction cap before state creation
Control -> OIDC: Authorization Code + PKCE S256\nstate + nonce + exact callback
OIDC -> AdminBrowser: Require phishing-resistant MFA
AdminBrowser -> OIDC: Authenticate with approved owner identity
OIDC --> AdminBrowser: Redirect with authorization code + state
AdminBrowser -> Control: GET /admin/oidc/callback
Control -> Control: Apply callback limits; atomically consume\nexact live state before one exchange
Control -> OIDC: Exchange code + PKCE verifier
OIDC --> Control: Signed ID token
Control -> Control: Validate issuer, audience, signature, time,\nnonce, exact owner subject, and MFA context
Control -> DB: Store digest of 256-bit session +\nsanitized authentication audit event
Control --> AdminBrowser: __Host-fga_admin Secure HttpOnly\nSameSite=Strict cookie + CSRF token

== Phase 1, Part 1 — Authorize FGA OAuth handler to use Flickr ==

Admin -> Secrets: Provision Flickr application key and consumer secret\nthrough provider-authenticated deployment controls
Control -> Secrets: Read configured/missing status only
Secrets --> Control: Non-secret version/status

opt Flickr user authorization is not already provisioned
  Admin -> AdminBrowser: Start administrative Flickr authorization
  AdminBrowser -> Control: POST Flickr authorization with\nsession + CSRF + recent authentication
  Control -> OAuth: Start Flickr OAuth authorization
  OAuth -> HostedDNS: Resolve www.flickr.com
  HostedDNS --> OAuth: www.flickr.com address records
  OAuth -> FlickrAPI: GET https://www.flickr.com/services/oauth/request_token\n(signed)
  FlickrAPI --> OAuth: Request token + token secret
  OAuth --> AdminBrowser: Redirect to\nhttps://www.flickr.com/services/oauth/authorize
  AdminBrowser -> FlickrAPI: GET https://www.flickr.com/services/oauth/authorize\nauthenticate and grant write access
  FlickrAPI --> AdminBrowser: Redirect to callback on flickrgroupaddr.com\nwith verifier
  AdminBrowser -> OAuth: GET https://flickrgroupaddr.com/{configured-oauth-callback-path}
  OAuth -> FlickrAPI: GET https://www.flickr.com/services/oauth/access_token\nwith verifier
  FlickrAPI --> OAuth: Access token + token secret + owner NSID
  OAuth -> FlickrAPI: Verify expected owner NSID + write permission
  FlickrAPI --> OAuth: Complete successful token status
  OAuth -> Secrets: Stage token + token secret under new version
  OAuth -> DB: Atomically activate secret reference + owner NSID\n+ sanitized administrative audit event
end

== Phase 1, Part 2 — Create a Lightroom installation identity ==

Admin -> AdminBrowser: On target workstation, open clean private window\nVerify clipboard history/sync off
Admin -> AdminBrowser: Select Create Plugin Code
AdminBrowser -> API: POST /api/v001/plugin-codes\nwith session + CSRF + recent authentication
API -> API: Generate 32 random octets with CSPRNG\nEncode canonical 13-group Crockford Base32 Plugin Code
API -> API: Compute unsalted SHA2-256 credential digest\n(no appended HMAC tag)
API -> DB: Atomically store digest, user, installation, active state\n+ sanitized administrative audit event
API --> AdminBrowser: Five-minute in-memory transfer view\nReturn clear-text Plugin Code exactly once
Admin -> AdminBrowser: Copy Plugin Code
AdminBrowser -> Clipboard: Write Plugin Code on explicit user gesture
note over Admin,Plugin
  This registers an installation identity, not the plug-in binary.
  Download/install may happen before or after provisioning;
  the credential is required before activation.
end note

== Phase 2 — Browser-free Lightroom activation ==

note over ClientDNS,Passwords
  Starting assumptions: Windows has Internet connectivity; all relevant
  DNS caches are empty; Lightroom Classic and the FGA LrC plug-in are installed;
  and LrPasswords contains no FGA credential.
end note

User -> LrC: Launch Lightroom Classic
LrC -> Plugin: Load FGA LrC plug-in
Plugin -> Passwords: Read installation credential
Passwords --> Plugin: No value
Plugin --> User: Show credential-generation URL on flickrgroupaddr.com\nand clear-text canonical Plugin Code input
User -> Plugin: Paste administratively issued credential
Clipboard --> Plugin: Current credential value
Plugin --> User: Show same grouping and typography\nfor side-by-side comparison with browser
Plugin -> Plugin: Validate exact canonical spelling\nNo case, alias, whitespace, or hyphen repair
Plugin -> Passwords: Store credential
Plugin -> Plugin: Clear visible field and ordinary-memory copies when practical

Plugin -> ClientDNS: Resolve flickrgroupaddr.com
alt Client DNS cache miss
  ClientDNS -> RecursiveDNS: Query A and/or AAAA records
  RecursiveDNS --> ClientDNS: Addresses + TTL
  ClientDNS -> ClientDNS: Cache records until TTL
else Client DNS cache hit
  ClientDNS -> ClientDNS: Return cached records
end
ClientDNS --> Plugin: Reachable FGA addresses
Plugin -> API: Establish HTTPS/TLS connection\nto https://flickrgroupaddr.com
note over Plugin,API
  Adobe documents HTTPS but no TLS-version contract or selector.
  The negotiated version is an implementation detail.
  Owner target: TLS 1.3+ edge if the latest Creative Cloud LrC
  on the adopted latest production/stable Windows passes its probe.
end note
Plugin -> API: GET https://flickrgroupaddr.com/api/v001/installations/current\nAuthorization: Bearer <installation credential>\nNo body or query
API -> API: Parse request and Bearer credential
  alt Malformed request envelope, body, or query
    API --> Plugin: 400 Bad Request; invalid_request
  else Authentication missing
    API --> Plugin: 401 Unauthorized; bare Bearer challenge
  else One Bearer token presented
    API -> API: Validate Bearer token wire grammar
    alt Malformed token value
      API --> Plugin: 401 Unauthorized; invalid_token
    else Canonical token value
      API -> API: Compute SHA2-256 digest
      API -> DB: Find digest and active installation
      DB --> API: Stored credential_class + FGA user + linked Flickr NSID
      API -> API: Match exact stored class/route allowlist\nDefault branch rejects
      alt Unknown credential/class, inactive, expired, revoked,\ndisabled, mismatch, or verification failure
        API --> Plugin: 401 Unauthorized; invalid_token
      else Active lrc_plugin credential authorized for route
        API --> Plugin: 200 OK + Cache-Control: no-store\n{schemaVersion: 1, installationId, installationRevision,\ninstallationState: active, presentedCredentialState: current}
        Plugin -> Plugin: Mark FGA connection authenticated
        Plugin --> User: Connected (no secret)
        User -> AdminBrowser: Erase transfer view
        AdminBrowser -> Clipboard: Overwrite with fixed non-secret text
        AdminBrowser -> AdminBrowser: Erase UI reference and close private window
      end
    end
end

note over Plugin,API
  Stored credential_class lrc_plugin is authoritative and independently checked.
  No request field creates or broadens it, and the response omits it.
  A pending candidate may read the resource with pending_rotation state only.
  The reusable HTTPS connection may remain open after the response.
end note

== Phase 3 — Paginated writable-group discovery ==

Plugin -> API: GET https://flickrgroupaddr.com/api/v001/\ngroups?page_size=100\nAuthorization: Bearer <installation credential>
API -> API: Validate Bearer grammar and compute SHA2-256\nLook up active installation by digest\nResolve linked FGA user + Flickr NSID
API -> API: Require page_size 1..100\nInitial request has no revision or keyset boundary
API -> DB: Read current snapshot + refresh state
alt Snapshot stale or missing and refresh admitted
  API -> DB: Create or join one per-user refresh job
  RefreshWorker -> HostedDNS: Resolve www.flickr.com
  HostedDNS --> RefreshWorker: www.flickr.com address records
  RefreshWorker -> Secrets: Read linked user's Flickr application secret,\nOAuth access token, and OAuth token secret
  Secrets --> RefreshWorker: Linked user's scoped OAuth material
  loop Flickr pages inside one bounded job
    RefreshWorker -> RefreshWorker: Generate fresh OAuth nonce and timestamp\nSign exact GET and normalized parameters\nHMAC-SHA1 (HMAC using SHA1-160)
    RefreshWorker -> FlickrAPI: GET https://www.flickr.com/services/rest/\n?method=flickr.groups.pools.getGroups&page=n&per_page=400\n&format=json&nojsoncallback=1\nOAuth key + token + nonce + timestamp + signature
    FlickrAPI --> RefreshWorker: One bounded writable-group page
    RefreshWorker -> DB: Validate and store reduced staging rows
  end
  RefreshWorker -> DB: Atomically replace current rows\nAdvance snapshotRevision + refreshedAt
end

alt No successful snapshot and refresh active
  API --> Plugin: 202 Accepted + Retry-After\nNo group array
else No successful snapshot and refresh failed
  API --> Plugin: 503 group_refresh_unavailable\nNo group array
else Last good snapshot available
  API -> DB: Read at most page_size rows\nOrder by exact Flickr group ID
  DB --> API: Groups page + whether another page remains
  API --> Plugin: 200 OK + revision + status\nGroups + nextAfterGroupId
  loop While nextAfterGroupId is non-null
    Plugin -> API: GET groups?page_size=100\n&snapshot_revision=r&after_group_id=last\nAuthorization: Bearer <installation credential>
    API -> API: Independently authenticate continuation
    API -> DB: Require current revision r\nRead IDs strictly greater than last
    alt Revision remains current
      DB --> API: Next keyset page
      API --> Plugin: 200 OK + groups page\nnextAfterGroupId or null
    else Revision changed
      API --> Plugin: 409 snapshot_changed\nNo group array; restart once
    end
  end
end

note over RefreshWorker,DB
  One active job per user; at most one start per 60 seconds.
  Limits: 25 Flickr pages, 10,000 groups, 2 MiB per response,
  and 60 seconds. Failure leaves the last good snapshot unchanged.
end note

Plugin --> User: Display completed aggregate by name; retain IDs as identity

== Phase 4 — Per-photo selection, render, and preflight ==

User -> LrC: Create or select FGA published collection
alt New album
  User -> LrC: Right-click FGA publish service -> Create Album...
  LrC -> Plugin: Create local published collection; no remote album ID yet
  note over LrC,Plugin
    Flickr photosets.create requires a primary Flickr photo ID.
    The first real successful upload can materialize the remote album.
  end note
else Existing album
  User -> LrC: Select existing FGA album
end
User -> LrC: Add culling candidates to album; remove rejects
User -> Plugin: Open Select Flickr Groups for selected photos
Plugin -> LrC: Read existing remote publish IDs
Plugin -> Recovery: Read retained common photo-binding IDs
loop Each selected photo with an FGA photo binding
  Plugin -> API: GET /api/v001/photo-bindings/<binding ID>/group-memberships
  API -> DB: Require binding ownership; derive photo and linked account
  DB --> API: Bound photo identity + owner
  API -> FlickrAPI: Signed GET flickr.photos.getAllContexts
  FlickrAPI --> API: Candidate visible sets and pools
  API -> API: Require stat=ok + explicit pool array\nValidate every bounded pool ID/title; no filtering/default
  alt Missing, non-array, partial, duplicate, malformed, or over budget
    API --> Plugin: 503 membership_observation_unavailable\nNo groups, observedAt, or keyset state
    Plugin --> User: Membership Unavailable\nDisable add confirmation for this photo
  else Complete validated observation
    API -> DB: Atomically replace current pool rows\nAdvance observationRevision + observedAt
    API --> Plugin: Current pool page + revision\nnextAfterGroupId
    loop While nextAfterGroupId is non-null
      Plugin -> API: GET membership page with\nobservation_revision + after_group_id
      API -> DB: Require current observation revision\nRead next group-ID keyset page
      API --> Plugin: Current pool page or\n409 membership_observation_changed
    end
  end
end
Plugin --> User: Read-only current Flickr groups + selectable additions
User -> Plugin: Confirm additional per-photo group targets
Plugin -> Recovery: Persist editable group-addition selections
opt Photo already has an FGA Flickr remote ID
  Plugin -> Recovery: Snapshot photo-binding ID + current verification revision\n+ new group IDs
  note over Plugin,API
    Continue directly at Phase 6.
    Do not render or upload the image again.
  end note
end
User -> LrC: Invoke native Publish Now for selected work or album pending work
LrC -> Plugin: Supply photos needing initial publication
Plugin -> Plugin: Snapshot each confirmed zero-or-more group set
Plugin -> Plugin: Treat every photo as independent

loop Each photo; no cross-photo order guarantee
  Plugin -> Recovery: Persist Lightroom UUID + selected group IDs
  Plugin -> LrC: Request configured rendition
  LrC --> Plugin: Completed rendered file
  Plugin -> Plugin: Verify readable, nonzero, and within size policy

  alt Render or preflight fails
    Plugin --> User: Stop this photo before signing or upload
  else Render passes preflight
    == Phase 5 — Direct Flickr upload signed by FGA API backend ==

    Plugin -> API: POST https://flickrgroupaddr.com/api/v001/\nupload-authorizations\nAuthorization: Bearer <installation credential>\n+ allowlisted metadata
    API -> API: Verify installation and validate complete request
    API -> DB: Require linked-user and deployment\nFlickr write gates enabled
    DB --> API: Both gate revisions enabled
    API -> Secrets: Read Flickr signing secrets
    Secrets --> API: Scoped secret values
    API -> API: Generate OAuth nonce, timestamp, and authorization ID
    API -> API: Sign exact non-file Flickr metadata
    API -> DB: Store record keyed by authorization ID\nwith null Flickr photo ID
    API --> Plugin: 200 OK + no-store signed upload envelope
    Plugin -> Recovery: Persist authorization ID only
    Plugin -> Plugin: Keep OAuth header and signed metadata only in memory

    Plugin -> ClientDNS: Resolve up.flickr.com
    alt Upload-host cache miss
      ClientDNS -> RecursiveDNS: Query A and/or AAAA records
      RecursiveDNS --> ClientDNS: Flickr upload addresses + TTL
      ClientDNS -> ClientDNS: Cache records until TTL
    else Upload-host cache hit
      ClientDNS -> ClientDNS: Return cached records
    end
    ClientDNS --> Plugin: Reachable Flickr upload addresses
    Plugin -> FlickrUpload: TLS handshake for up.flickr.com
    FlickrUpload --> Plugin: Certificate chain
    Plugin -> Plugin: Validate hostname, chain, and dates
    Plugin -> FlickrUpload: POST https://up.flickr.com/services/upload/\nexact signed metadata + rendered file as photo part
    note over Plugin,FlickrUpload
      The FGA LrC plug-in streams image bytes through LrHttp.postMultipart
      directly to Flickr.
      The FGA API backend never receives them. Flickr signs non-file metadata,
      not the binary photo part.
    end note

    alt Definitive Flickr rejection
      FlickrUpload --> Plugin: Rejection with known failure
      Plugin --> User: Report failure; fresh authorization required for retry
    else Upload call has no definitive result
      FlickrUpload -x Plugin: Timeout or connection loss after\nLrHttp.postMultipart was invoked
      Plugin -> Recovery: Set upload_outcome_unknown
      Plugin --> User: Require reconciliation; do not auto-upload again
    else Flickr accepts upload
      FlickrUpload --> Plugin: Flickr photo ID
      Plugin -> Recovery: Persist Flickr photo ID before\nLightroom Classic catalog remote ID
      Plugin -> LrC: recordPublishedPhotoId(Flickr photo ID)
      Plugin -> Recovery: Persist album_attachment_pending for\ncollection's one-to-one Flickr album
      note over Plugin,Recovery
        Album attachment is an eventual per-photo obligation.
        It is not atomic with upload or ordered across photos.
        Ticket #0060 defines the documented Flickr operation and recovery.
      end note

      Plugin -> API: PUT /api/v001/upload-authorizations/<authorization ID>/photo-binding\n+ exact Flickr photo ID + Authorization: Bearer <installation credential>
      API -> FlickrAPI: Signed flickr.photos.getInfo for exact photo ID
      FlickrAPI --> API: Complete photo ID + owner NSID
      API -> API: Validate exact ID, linked owner, and current link revision
      API -> DB: Commit common binding unique to (FGA user, Flickr photo ID)
      DB --> API: Binding ID + verification revision
      API --> Plugin: 201 created or 200 matching binding
      Plugin -> Recovery: Persist binding ID + verification revision

      == Phase 6 — Durable group-intent handoff ==

      opt Selected group snapshot is nonempty
        Plugin -> API: One POST https://flickrgroupaddr.com/api/v001/\ngroup-submission-batches\nAuthorization: Bearer <installation credential>\n+ schema v2 binding ID/revision + complete bounded unique group-ID set
        API -> API: Verify installation and complete batch\nNo client photo ID; no single-group alias; no client slicing
        API -> DB: Require owned current binding/revisions\nDerive Flickr photo ID, FGA user, owner, source, and link
        API -> DB: Begin one transaction; recheck binding revisions
        loop Each selected Flickr group ID
          API -> DB: Ensure unique (photo ID, group ID) intent exists\n+ in (FGA user, group ID) FIFO partition
        end
        API -> DB: Commit transaction
        DB --> API: Durable intent snapshots
        par Success acknowledgement
          API --> Plugin: 202 Accepted + binding + ordered intent snapshots
          Plugin -> Recovery: Mark local outbox complete
        else Courtesy-bounded immediate progress
          API -> GroupWorker: Zero or one best-effort hint per batch after commit\ncanonical-lowest newly eligible partition ID + wake revision only
          note over API,GroupWorker
            The request handler makes no Flickr call and emits no per-group fan-out.
            Every other due partition remains indexed for the scheduled sweep.
          end note
        end
      end
    end
  end
end

== Phase 7 — Hosted queue progress after durable acceptance ==

Scheduler -> GroupWorker: Start indexed due-work sweep\nat least once per minute
GroupWorker -> DB: Claim one due partition by database clock\nnew lease ID + incremented fencing generation
DB --> GroupWorker: Current lease generation + active FIFO head
GroupWorker -> DB: Check linked-user and deployment Flickr write gates
DB --> GroupWorker: Both gate revisions enabled
note over GroupWorker,DB
  Active FIFO states: queued, attempting, retrying, throttled.
  Terminal rows remain durable but are excluded from queue membership.
  A paused scope is excluded from scheduling; its intents remain unchanged.
  Every worker mutation checks the lease ID + generation.
  Lost/duplicate hints and expired leases converge through the due sweep.
end note
GroupWorker -> DB: Check permanent block for exact photo/group pair
alt Permanent block exists
  DB --> GroupWorker: Existing terminal block
  GroupWorker -> DB: Preserve terminal row/history;\nexclude active queue; make no Flickr write
else Pair is not blocked
  GroupWorker -> HostedDNS: Resolve www.flickr.com if needed
  HostedDNS --> GroupWorker: www.flickr.com address records
  GroupWorker -> Secrets: Read scoped Flickr signing secrets
  Secrets --> GroupWorker: Scoped secret values
  GroupWorker -> GroupWorker: Atomically reserve Flickr rate-limit capacity\nfor membership GET, getInfo, and possible pools.add
  GroupWorker -> FlickrAPI: GET https://www.flickr.com/services/rest/\nmethod=flickr.photos.getAllContexts + photo ID
  alt Membership unavailable or incomplete
    FlickrAPI --> GroupWorker: No complete usable membership observation
    GroupWorker -> DB: Keep FIFO head retrying; send no getInfo/add\nPersist safe-read failure + bounded next attempt
  else Exact target group is present
    FlickrAPI --> GroupWorker: Complete membership contains target group
    GroupWorker -> DB: Terminal added from pre-add observation\nRemove active queue membership; send no getInfo/add
  else Complete observation omits target group
    FlickrAPI --> GroupWorker: Complete target-absent observation
    GroupWorker -> FlickrAPI: GET https://www.flickr.com/services/rest/\nmethod=flickr.groups.getInfo + group ID
    alt Transient/unknown preflight failure or moderation value is uninterpretable
      FlickrAPI --> GroupWorker: No usable ispoolmoderated observation
      GroupWorker -> DB: Keep FIFO head retrying; send no add request\nPersist failure count + next_attempt_not_before\n30-60 s initial window; bounded progression to 8-15 min cap
    else Definitive linked-user or deployment fault
      FlickrAPI --> GroupWorker: Auth, signing, key, method, format, or protocol result
      GroupWorker -> DB: Pause applicable durable gate; retain active head;\nsend no add request; emit one alert per pause revision
    else Documented permanent request-specific result
      FlickrAPI --> GroupWorker: Explicit request-specific preflight result
      GroupWorker -> DB: Set terminal needs_attention\nRemove active queue membership; send no add request
    else Fresh moderation observation
      FlickrAPI --> GroupWorker: ispoolmoderated = 0 or 1
      GroupWorker -> DB: Record moderation value/time and attempt
      GroupWorker -> GroupWorker: Check monotonic preflight age
      alt Age reached 1,000 ms before POST dispatch
        GroupWorker -> DB: Discard observation; repeat preflight\nwithout sending add request
      else Age remains under 1,000 ms
        GroupWorker -> DB: Recheck both gate revisions and\nmark dispatch_started durably
        GroupWorker -> GroupWorker: Recheck monotonic age immediately after commit
        alt Age now reached 1,000 ms and no bytes were sent
          GroupWorker -> DB: Record not_dispatched_preflight_expired;\nrepeat preflight
        else Age remains under 1,000 ms
          GroupWorker -> FlickrAPI: POST https://www.flickr.com/services/rest/\nmethod=flickr.groups.pools.add + photo ID + group ID
        alt Photo added (stat=ok) or photo already in pool (code 3)
          FlickrAPI --> GroupWorker: Added or already in pool
          GroupWorker -> DB: Terminal added; retain row/history;\nremove active queue membership
        else Photo added to pending queue (code 6) or already pending (code 7)
          FlickrAPI --> GroupWorker: Entered or already in moderation queue
          GroupWorker -> DB: Permanently block exact pair\n+ terminal moderation_submitted\n+ remove active queue membership
          opt Photo added to pending queue (code 6) contradicts observed ispoolmoderated=0
            GroupWorker -> DB: Record moderation race/upstream inconsistency
          end
        else User's pool submission limit reached (code 5)
          FlickrAPI --> GroupWorker: User's group submission limit reached
          GroupWorker -> DB: Atomically and durably throttle only this user/group partition\nRecord result + observation + next probe time\nCommit before releasing partition lease
        else Service unavailable (code 105) or temporary write failure (code 106)
          FlickrAPI --> GroupWorker: Explicit temporary failure
          GroupWorker -> DB: Retain head for bounded-backoff retry\nwith a new preflight
        else Other documented application code
          FlickrAPI --> GroupWorker: Permanent, auth, or configuration result
          GroupWorker -> DB: Apply explicit documented class;\npause linked-user or deployment gate when scoped
        else Unknown code, or dispatch_started without zero-byte proof and definitive durable result
          GroupWorker -> DB: Permanently block exact pair\n+ terminal delivery_uncertain\n+ remove active queue membership; never retry\nUnknown code also pauses deployment gate
        end
      end
    end
  end
  end
end

note over GroupWorker,FlickrAPI
  The membership observation is advisory, and the required getInfo and pools.add calls are not atomic.
  The FGA group-submission worker starts POST dispatch under 1,000 ms after receiving getInfo,
  but cannot bound network/Flickr processing. The add result is authoritative.
  The FGA API backend and LrC plug-in provide no force-resubmit path.
end note

note over API,GroupWorker
  A Flickr write gate prevents new starts but cannot recall an already-dispatched request.
  Resume has no timer or bypass: the FGA administrative control plane verifies
  the expected gate revision with a fresh non-mutating OAuth token check, records
  the repair evidence, and enables the revision by compare-and-set.
end note

== Phase 8 — Additional photos and final state ==

note over User,ClientDNS
  The plug-in never launches or controls the client browser. Windows DNS
  contains only temporary name-resolution records. DNS TTL expiry does not
  invalidate an established connection. Reuse is limited to the same exact
  origin while the owning HTTP stack retains the connection as eligible after
  consuming the prior response. For another request, a missing, closed,
  close-directed, incomplete-response, failed, timed-out, or policy-retired
  connection requires applicable DNS resolution and a new TLS handshake and
  validation. The Lightroom Classic host may close after the 202 response;
  the FGA group-submission worker continues from the FGA database.
end note

note over API,DB
  FGA policy calls an image "in Flickr" only after a complete stat=ok
  flickr.photos.getInfo result for its exact photo ID and expected owner
  is committed with an observation time. The upload response alone is insufficient.
end note

@enduml
